<title>BELGIUM: EU clears German pensions management venture.</title>
<headline>EU clears German pensions management venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it had approved a proposed joint venture between Deutsche Beamten Lebensversicherung AG, which belongs to German insurance group DBV-Winterthur, and German life insurer Gothaer Lebensversicherung AG to manage corporate pensions in Germany.</p>
<p>The Commission noted that the market was still in its formative stages in in Germany and characterised by strong competition. It therefore cleared the deal.</p>
<p>The joint venture will be called Gothaer Pensions-Management GmbH and it will have a share of the German market &quot;well below 10 percent&quot;, the Copmmission said in a statement.</p>
</text>
